1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,256
How many people use your assistant?

2
00:00:03,256 --> 00:00:05,181
Does it solve their problems?

3
00:00:05,181 --> 00:00:08,702
Do they like the answers, and what did it learn from them?

4
00:00:08,702 --> 00:00:11,068
This video shows the AI chat reports:

5
00:00:11,068 --> 00:00:16,239
the Session Analytics report, the Extracted Data report and the Conversion Goals report,

6
00:00:16,239 --> 00:00:18,330
and the settings that fill them.

7
00:00:22,930 --> 00:00:25,291
How much is it used, and when?

8
00:00:25,291 --> 00:00:28,374
How long are the chats, and who has them:

9
00:00:28,374 --> 00:00:31,260
signed-in users or anonymous visitors?

10
00:00:32,010 --> 00:00:33,951
Does it solve the problem?

11
00:00:33,951 --> 00:00:37,650
The AI can judge each finished chat as resolved or not.

12
00:00:38,400 --> 00:00:39,911
Do people like it?

13
00:00:39,911 --> 00:00:44,760
A thumbs up or thumbs down on an answer feeds the satisfaction figures.

14
00:00:45,510 --> 00:00:48,335
What did it collect, such as an email address?

15
00:00:48,335 --> 00:00:52,300
And did a chat reach the goals that you set, such as a booked demo?

16
00:00:56,499 --> 00:01:00,854
The reports hold only what was collected, and only from the moment that

17
00:01:00,854 --> 00:01:02,607
collection was turned on.

18
00:01:02,607 --> 00:01:06,679
Open a chat profile, and open its Data Processing and Metrics tab.

19
00:01:07,131 --> 00:01:12,315
Enable session metrics collects the numbers, and adds thumbs up and thumbs down

20
00:01:12,315 --> 00:01:14,084
buttons to the answers.

21
00:01:14,084 --> 00:01:19,391
Enable AI resolution detection lets the AI judge if each chat solved the problem.

22
00:01:19,841 --> 00:01:25,375
Enable conversion metrics scores each chat against your goals, and Enable data extraction

23
00:01:25,375 --> 00:01:27,763
collects the details that you name.

24
00:01:27,763 --> 00:01:32,657
A chat counts as finished after its inactivity timeout, and the results appear

25
00:01:32,657 --> 00:01:34,171
a few minutes later.

26
00:01:38,378 --> 00:01:43,597
Open Reports, Artificial Intelligence Reports, and AI Chat Session Analytics.

27
00:01:43,597 --> 00:01:47,811
Choose a Date range, such as the last 30 days, and a profile,

28
00:01:47,811 --> 00:01:50,138
or any profile, and click Show.

29
00:01:50,589 --> 00:01:55,649
Conversation and Usage shows the Total Sessions and the Unique Visitors, the Containment

30
00:01:55,649 --> 00:02:00,170
Rate, the share of chats that the assistant handled alone, and the Abandonment

31
00:02:00,170 --> 00:02:03,669
Rate, the share where the person left without a resolution.

32
00:02:04,119 --> 00:02:08,699
It also shows how long chats last and how many messages they have,

33
00:02:08,699 --> 00:02:10,989
and how many people come back.

34
00:02:10,989 --> 00:02:15,759
Resolved, Abandoned and Active Sessions count the chats by their end.

35
00:02:16,211 --> 00:02:19,275
The usage by time of day and by day of the week show

36
00:02:19,275 --> 00:02:23,291
when people chat, so that you can have staff ready for the busy hours.

37
00:02:23,741 --> 00:02:28,242
User Segmentation separates signed-in users from anonymous visitors.

38
00:02:28,242 --> 00:02:33,046
Model and System Performance shows the response time and the tokens used:

39
00:02:33,046 --> 00:02:37,851
the input tokens that are sent, and the output tokens that the AI writes.

40
00:02:38,302 --> 00:02:43,638
Resolution and Conversion shows how many finished chats the AI judged resolved, and

41
00:02:43,638 --> 00:02:46,216
the average score against your goals.

42
00:02:46,216 --> 00:02:48,435
User Feedback shows the thumbs:

43
00:02:48,435 --> 00:02:52,392
the satisfaction rate, and how many chats were rated at all.

44
00:02:52,843 --> 00:02:56,923
Export as CSV downloads the chats behind the report.

45
00:03:01,126 --> 00:03:06,265
Open Reports, Artificial Intelligence Reports, and AI Chat Extracted Data.

46
00:03:06,265 --> 00:03:10,569
It lists what the assistant collected, one row for each chat.

47
00:03:10,569 --> 00:03:14,616
Choose the AI profile, which is required, and click Show.

48
00:03:15,068 --> 00:03:19,562
Each row has the session date, the session ID, and one column for

49
00:03:19,562 --> 00:03:23,360
each detail that you named, such as the email address.

50
00:03:23,360 --> 00:03:26,778
Export as CSV is how leads reach another system.

51
00:03:30,979 --> 00:03:34,139
Open AI Chat Conversion Goals in the same menu.

52
00:03:34,139 --> 00:03:38,672
It shows how each finished chat scored against the goals that you set.

53
00:03:38,672 --> 00:03:42,429
Choose the AI profile, which is required, and click Show.

54
00:03:42,879 --> 00:03:47,442
Each row has the session date, the session ID, the total points, and

55
00:03:47,442 --> 00:03:49,353
one column for each goal.

56
00:03:49,353 --> 00:03:54,039
Chats with a low score show where the assistant fails to guide people.

57
00:03:58,239 --> 00:04:00,167
Read some unresolved chats.

58
00:04:00,167 --> 00:04:04,139
They show the questions that your knowledge cannot answer yet.

59
00:04:04,889 --> 00:04:11,849
A high abandonment rate, or many thumbs down, points to instructions or knowledge that need work.

60
00:04:12,599 --> 00:04:17,113
Some AI services do not report tokens for every answer, so the token

61
00:04:17,113 --> 00:04:19,675
figures can be lower than your bill.

62
00:04:19,675 --> 00:04:23,639
The usage report is the place to compare with your invoice.

63
00:04:25,639 --> 00:04:29,435
Turn on the metrics, let the chats come in, and read the reports

64
00:04:29,435 --> 00:04:31,170
to improve your assistant.

65
00:04:31,170 --> 00:04:32,579
Thanks for watching.

